Description
The successful candidate will learn to carry out project management and administrative tasks, environmental impact assessments, reporting writing skills, networking and client relationship skills. The candidate will be required to perform day to day office administrative tasks.
Requirements
Assist in supporting the environmental legislative processes applicable to the relevant country, under the guidance of senior team members;
Stay informed about applicable environmental legislation and its potential implications on ongoing projects;
Support the team in maintaining high-quality standards in service delivery and project outputs;
Participate in selected marketing and business development activities, such as preparing presentation materials or attending meetings with senior staff;
Provide support to team management activities, including:
Assisting with resource tracking and workload planning.
Helping coordinates day-to-day office and project administration.
Assisting with budget-related documentation and forecasting tasks.
Supporting the onboarding and training of fellow interns or junior team members;
Gain practical exposure by supporting and observing the following project components:
Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs) in line with relevant legislation;
Environmental permitting and mining application processes;
Interdisciplinary collaboration with specialists;
Stakeholder and public consultation processes;
Monitoring of project schedules and budget compliance;
Liaison with clients and authorities;
Assist with compiling, formatting, and reviewing reports for submission to clients and regulatory bodies;
Participate in fieldwork assignments, including work in remote or physically demanding environments, under supervision;
Perform general administrative tasks to support the environmental team and contribute to the smooth running of projects.
Qualifications
Post graduate degree in Environmental Management or similar.
Driver's license is advantageous.
Other Requirements
Excellent attention to detail.
Strong customer-orientation.
Strong analytical problem-solving skills and experience.
Excellent ability to manage one’s time and meet tight deadlines.
Excellent organization skills.
Willingness to travel internationally.
Ability to build and maintain a strong network of relationships.
